---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-draft-card</code> is how the assistant's writes appear (ADR-000007: reads are free, writes
  are drafts). It shows the record the assistant prepared; nothing is saved until the person presses
  the confirm button. Press <strong>Raise incident</strong> in the demo.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-draft-card id='draft-demo' headline='New incident' supporting-text='IT service desk' confirm-label='Raise incident' style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'>
    <span slot='start' style='display: grid; place-items: center; inline-size: 2rem; block-size: 2rem; border-radius: var(--shape-corner-small); background: var(--color-blue-container); color: var(--color-on-blue-container); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.75rem;'>IT</span>
  </wc-draft-card>
  <wc-button id='draft-reset' variant='text' size='sm' style='margin-top: 0.75rem;'>Reset</wc-button>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var card = document.querySelector('#draft-demo');
      card.fields = [
        { label: 'Short description', value: 'Cracked screen on laptop LT-0412' },
        { label: 'Asset', value: 'LT-0412, assigned to you' },
        { label: 'Urgency', value: '3 · Medium', suggested: true, reason: "You didn't say you can't work. Make it High if you can't." },
      ];
      card.addEventListener('confirm', function () {
        card.state = 'submitting';
        setTimeout(function () {
          card.state = 'done';
          card.resultText = 'Raised INC-2318 in IT service desk';
          card.resultHref = '#inc-2318';
        }, 1000);
      });
      card.addEventListener('edit', function () {
        myConsole.log('edit: open the incident form with form.suggest()');
      });
      document.querySelector('#draft-reset').addEventListener('click', function () {
        card.state = 'draft';
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>States</h3>
<p>
  The buttons fire events and the app sets <code>state</code>: <code>submitting</code> while it saves,
  then <code>done</code> with <code>result-text</code> and <code>result-href</code>, or
  <code>error</code> with <code>error-text</code>. <code>discard</code> turns the card
  <code>discarded</code> unless the event is cancelled. <strong>Edit in form</strong> fires
  <code>edit</code>: open the app's own form, filled with the draft by <code>wc-form</code>'s
  <code>suggest()</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: grid; gap: 1rem; inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'>
    <wc-draft-card headline='New incident' supporting-text='IT service desk' state='error' error-text='Asset is required by IT service desk.' confirm-label='Raise incident'></wc-draft-card>
    <wc-draft-card headline='Leave request' supporting-text='Human resources' state='discarded'></wc-draft-card>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Irreversible drafts</h3>
<p>
  With <code>irreversible</code>, the confirm button is a danger button and asks again in a
  <code>wc-confirm-dialog</code> before firing <code>confirm</code>; <code>irreversible-text</code>
  says what can't be undone.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-draft-card id='draft-irreversible' headline='Remove Grace Hopper from Payroll' supporting-text='Administration' confirm-label='Remove access' irreversible irreversible-text='Grace loses access to Payroll right away.' style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'></wc-draft-card>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#draft-irreversible').addEventListener('confirm', function () {
      myConsole.log('confirm (after the second ask)');
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>When AI is off</h3>
<p>
  The card is the assistant's output, so it renders nothing while the page has AI off. The app's own
  form is always there for the same task.
</p>
